{
 "_what": "Option names PrusaSlicer 2.9.6 accepts, plus preset metadata keys it needs but does not list as options.",
 "_source": "Generated from `prusa-slicer --help-fff`, which is authoritative. Do NOT regenerate this from `strings` on the binary: that misses option names entirely and reports valid keys such as layer_height, perimeters and retract_length as unknown. Two earlier conclusions in this project were drawn that way and one of them was wrong.",
 "_metadata_note": "--help-fff lists SLICING options only, so preset metadata -- inherits, compatible_printers, host_type and friends -- is absent from it while being entirely valid in a preset file. That set is listed separately here rather than being inferred.",
 "_why": "SuperSlicer is the master format and has many options PrusaSlicer does not. Writing them into a PrusaSlicer preset is silently ignored at best; the ones that overlap by NAME but differ in UNITS are the dangerous case -- default_speed does not exist in PrusaSlicer, so every speed expressed as a percentage of it resolved against nothing and a Benchy came out at 2h27 against Orca's 33 minutes.",
